[86.421394, "i", "cat > /home/user/FIX_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\n=== CORRELATION SCRIPT FIX SUMMARY ===\n\nPROBLEM:\nThe correlate.py script was finding 0 lateral movement candidates (not 80% fewer, but 100% fewer)\nfrom Suricata eve.json logs, while the same logic worked with Zeek logs.\n\nROOT CAUSE - TWO CRITICAL BUGS:\n\n1. WRONG EVENT TYPE (Primary Bug):\n   - Script checked for event_type == \"netflow\"\n   - Suricata uses event_type == \"flow\"\n   - This caused the script to skip ALL flow events\n\n2. WRONG TIMESTAMP FORMAT:\n   - Script used: \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"\n   - Suricata format: \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%f%z\" (includes microseconds and timezone)\n   - This would have caused parsing errors once bug #1 was fixed\n\nFIXES APPLIED:\n- Line 24: Changed event_type check from \"netflow\" to \"flow\"\n- Line 15: Updated timestamp format to handle microseconds and timezone\n\nRESULTS:\n- Old script: 0 candidates detected\n- Fixed script: 1+ candidates detected (including 10.1.5.23)\n- Host 10.1.5.23 shows clear scanning behavior hitting multiple internal hosts\n  o"]
[86.421533, "i", "n ports 445, 3389, 5985, 135, 22 within short time windows\n\nThe correlation logic itself was correct - it was just never processing any events.\nEOF\n"]
